{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/762632-dev-appreciation-thread","id":762632,"title":"Dev appreciation thread.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-10T15:07:30-08:00","id":762632,"title":"Dev appreciation thread.","content":"As written in the title. <br /> <br /> So far I really love the courts system, especially Toronto as its a cool city.<br /> <br /> I like that were getting multiple courts and the tools to make more.<br /> <br /> I like the multiple possibly city setting approach, including along other WotC books a strong cross over city in Tokyo. It gives me all kinds of ideas.<br /> <br /> I loooove what they've with the seemings and kiths approach, especially Darklings which really emotional resenated with me. if they do decide to go with dual kith, there will be a huge amount of combos between Seeming/Kith/ second kith/court (and possibly entitlements).<br /> <br /> There approach to contracts will get rid of the weak ones you had to take to get higher ones, I like that.<br /> <br /> I like that changelings can get out of restraints by using magic now.<br /> <br /> I'm curious amd excited about how pledges will work.<br /> <br /> I'm glad goblin vows are in the core book now.<br /> <br /> I love what we know so far about Onieromamcy, and how Changelings can physically enter the dreams via the hedge.<br /> <br /> I like the Fae Touched, a flavourful, yet flexible mortal splat, but I'd give them a normal lifespan.<br /> <br /> I like that they're updating the rules to the 2e rule set.<br /> <br /> I like the huntsmen.<br /> <br /> I like the cult of Mithras<br /> <br /> The idea of Loyalist Seeming. I like the ideas for expanding the Seemings like Grimms and gamblers (or whatever they will be called).<br /> <br /> Did I miss anything else that's awesome?<br /> <br /> I'd like to thank the devs for all thier hard work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T14:28:05-08:00","id":763465,"title":"","content":"i agree that I enjoyed pretty much everything I've read thus far.<br /> <br /> The new Seemings allow for a lot more flavor, I think, and capture a concept that wasn't part of 1E - how/why the character escaped, and the effects it has on the character. I loved 1st Ed, of course, but the Seemings were more about why they were taken, which was then specified further in the Kits (along with what role they played in Arcadia). The new Seeming/Kith system, and the separation between them, make more sense to me,and provide more room for exploration.<br /> <br /> But more than that, I think that the new Court system, and making it more flexible from the gate rather than adding in extra courts in later supplements makes the setting feel much more robust and complete from the get-go; beyond that, having a demonstration of court and city construction makes coming up with new systems that much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:35:11-08:00","id":763680,"title":"","content":"So far I'm loving all the changeling 2e stuff. It's the most I've ever read about changeling and I'm looking forward to doing a full read through of this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T04:16:19-08:00","id":763941,"title":"","content":"I also love Onyx Path approach to game development in general. <br /> <br /> I've said it else where, but I'd love to see WotC contract 5e and the D&amp;D settings like the Forgotten Realms to Onyx Path the way White Wolf has.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I'll make seperate thread for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T11:57:48-08:00","id":768640,"title":"","content":"The open development style is pretty damn great. Really do wish more companies would try that (that is kind of why I tend to latch onto more third party producers than first party ones in D&amp;D at this point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:16:42-08:00","id":769317,"title":"","content":"i think one of the problems with the open development approach to game design is that it doesn't take much for projects to appear stalled. <br /> <br /> like changeling 2e. <br /> <br /> i'm sure that it is doing fine. but the initial massive weeks long info dump and developer interaction with the audience set an expectation for the development process which may have been a little unrealistic to maintain. i am not super active on these forums, but i visit periodically to see if there is any new and interesting topics, and it would be easy to assume if one is not familiar with the creative process that the game is in a hold pattern.<br /> <br /> that being said, i have enjoyed a lot of things discussed in the open development threads. i feel that the game that is being made will be well crafted and explore changelings in cool and interesting ways!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:11:57-08:00","id":769416,"title":"","content":"I'm sure very thing will be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T23:01:15-08:00","id":770551,"title":"","content":"I'm getting the impression that things like Talecrafting and Oneiromancy will be much more central to the game in 2e, which is something I'm looking forward to.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Bulwark ritual and Approaches a lot. Lots of story potential there.<br /> <br /> The new approach to Seemings, though a little jarring when you're used to 1st ed, is quite novel. I think it will spark some cool character concepts and drive some good rp.<br /> <br /> Kiths pack a lot more punch now, which is cool. Also, decoupling Kith and Seeming is awesome!<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to reading 2e. (I'm looking forward to running it, too, but since my current chronicle wouldn't convert well, it'll be awhile until I get the chance. Which makes me sad.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T12:46:32-08:00","id":777862,"title":"","content":"Just in general, I like how all the different splats are starting to look more like their own unique entities in 2nd edition, compared to first where they were all, basically, cookie-cutter copies of one another. Like now, they all share mechanics, but there are differences giving them all a lot more personality, and that's been coming through in changeling too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:28:29-08:00","id":781883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/762632-dev-appreciation-thread?p=770551#post770551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting the impression that things like Talecrafting and Oneiromancy will be much more central to the game in 2e, which is something I'm looking forward to.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Bulwark ritual and Approaches a lot. Lots of story potential there.<br /> <br /> The new approach to Seemings, though a little jarring when you're used to 1st ed, is quite novel. I think it will spark some cool character concepts and drive some good rp.<br /> <br /> Kiths pack a lot more punch now, which is cool. Also, decoupling Kith and Seeming is awesome!<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to reading 2e. (I'm looking forward to running it, too, but since my current chronicle wouldn't convert well, it'll be awhile until I get the chance. Which makes me sad.)</div> </div> </div> </div>where have we heard anything about tale crafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:00:15-08:00","id":781908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/762632-dev-appreciation-thread?p=781883#post781883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where have we heard anything about tale crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-court-creation-and-toronto/\" target=\"_blank\">Court Creation</a>. Every Court gets affinity for the Contract of Talespinning, which suggests at least a nominal connection with the stuff talecrafting handled in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:38:32-08:00","id":781933,"title":"","content":"I'm still new to the game, but what I've read so far makes the courts feel more immediately interesting and relevant than when I read my 1e pdfs. To be fair, I've been updating the background for my character concept, and having the Beast's new blessing in throwing off human conventions has got me imagining an abruptly disinhibited hedonist going into the Spring court. I think the changes are helping me grow my character concept more organically.<br /> <br /> I should take another look at the court creation thread. Someone brought up the topic of a Tarot themed court, which had occurred to me before I started reading the forums. I should also refresh my memory on the Fool's Journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:48:20-08:00","id":782830,"title":"","content":"So talecrafting which was its own mechnic in 1e, might have become talespinner the court contract (or contracts if thier are court variations of the talespinning contracts like thier is for the contracts of emotion.)<br /> <br /> Or perhaps talecrafting remains it own mechnic, but talespinning contract modifies it somehow, the contract of dreams did to onieromancy in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T18:18:59-08:00","id":788436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/762632-dev-appreciation-thread?p=769317#post769317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think one of the problems with the open development approach to game design is that it doesn't take much for projects to appear stalled.<br /> <br /> like changeling 2e.<br /> <br /> i'm sure that it is doing fine. but the initial massive weeks long info dump and developer interaction with the audience set an expectation for the development process which may have been a little unrealistic to maintain. i am not super active on these forums, but i visit periodically to see if there is any new and interesting topics, and it would be easy to assume if one is not familiar with the creative process that the game is in a hold pattern.<br /> <br /> that being said, i have enjoyed a lot of things discussed in the open development threads. i feel that the game that is being made will be well crafted and explore changelings in cool and interesting ways!</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a little stalled for a bit. I had a serious, crippling bout with depression. I was hospitalised for it. Then, basically as soon as I got out of that, I contracted a really awful case of pneumonia, for which I was hospitalised again. I'm out now, and trying to get caught up. <br /> <br /> But, I'm in a draft right now, making it sing. <br /> <br /> Also? Thank you guys for all the awesome kind words. I hope the game is as good as some of you expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T14:13:59-08:00","id":788956,"title":"","content":"Good to read you got out of the Hedge again David. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I\u00b4m patient and look forward when 2ed of Lost will be published. <br /> <br /> Be patient with yourself and remember: Depression lies! <br /> <br /> I didn\u00b4t you can make a draft sing - but again - this is so thematic for changeling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T17:22:47-08:00","id":789030,"title":"","content":"Making a draft sing... Suddenly, I'm imagining a singing beer mug. Also appropriately thematic.<br /> <br /> Anyway, glad to hear you're back from all that. Once had a vertigo/anxiety attack brought on by excessive introspection that made me discover a talent for haiku, myself.<br /> <br /> Here comes Wonderland.<br /> I need to stop chasing him:<br /> <b>I'm</b> the White Rabbit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://recursiverabbit.com/\" target=\"_blank\">~Recursive Rabbit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T20:18:39-08:00","id":792920,"title":"","content":"It's funny how much one sentence about the game can excite you so much. All it took was seeing this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/626312-open-development-where-is-it-at-right-now-and-what-do-you-want-to-see-soon?p=636934#post636934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Oneiromancy will be tied to paths in the Hedge).</div> </div> </div> </div>...to get me eagerly waiting to read Changeling 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T16:34:19-08:00","id":793309,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear your feeling better Dave. For my emotional issues I like ACT (Acceptance and Commitment theapy), I don't know if it will help you or not, just something you might choose to look into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T17:19:40-08:00","id":793857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/762632-dev-appreciation-thread?p=793309#post793309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to hear your feeling better Dave. For my emotional issues I like ACT (Acceptance and Commitment theapy), I don't know if it will help you or not, just something you might choose to look into.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good friend of mine works as a psychologist. She comes from a Cognitive Behavioural Therapy background but has recently started to include some ACT elements for her clients and says it's had some very positive results. With these things sometimes it's just a matter of finding what's the right match for you, but ACT definitely sounds like it helps a lot of people so it might be worth a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}